export const helpCategories = [{"id":"getting-started","label":"Getting Started","labelHa":"Farawa","order":1},{"id":"everyday","label":"Everyday tasks","labelHa":"Ayyukan yau da kullum","order":2},{"id":"operations","label":"Operations","labelHa":"Ayyuka","order":3},{"id":"configuration","label":"Configuration","labelHa":"Saiti","order":4},{"id":"insights","label":"Insights & tools","labelHa":"Bayanai da kayan aiki","order":5},{"id":"troubleshooting","label":"Troubleshooting","labelHa":"Warware matsaloli","order":6}]
export const helpGuides = [{"slug":"set-up-your-shop","title":"Set up your shop","summary":"Go from sign-up to your first sale in about 5 minutes.","category":"getting-started","order":1,"keywords":["register","sign up","signup","create account","create store","new account","onboarding","approval","verify","otp","location","pin","map","hours","first product","getting started","start selling","open my shop","new merchant"],"body":"# Set up your shop\n\nWelcome to Logistics Platform! This guide takes you from sign-up all the way to your first\nsale - it only takes about **5 minutes**. You'll create your account, get\napproved, pin your shop on the map, set your hours, and add your first product.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Create your account\n\nOn the sign-up page, tap **\"Register as a Merchant\"** and fill in the three short\nsteps:\n\n![Sign up - your personal details (step 1 of 3)](/help/screenshots/merchant/01-signup-step1.png)\n\n- **Step 1 - About you:** your first name, last name, email, phone number, and a\n  password (at least 8 characters).\n- **Step 2 - About your business:** pick the **category** that fits your shop\n  (Food, Pharmacy, Groceries, and so on), then your business name and contact.\n- **Step 3 - Your hours:** set the times you open and close.\n\nThen tap **\"Complete Registration.\"**\n\n> 💡 **Tip:** Use a phone number you actually answer - it's how customers and\n> riders reach you about orders.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Verify your email\n\nWe send a **6-digit code** to the email you signed up with. Type it into the\n**\"Verification Code\"** box and tap **\"Verify Email.\"**\n\n![Enter the 6-digit code we email you](/help/screenshots/merchant/02-verify-email.png)\n\n> 💡 **Didn't get it?** Wait a minute, check your spam folder, then tap\n> **\"Resend code\"** (you can resend once every 60 seconds).\n\n---\n\n## 3. Wait for approval\n\nAfter you verify, your account is **reviewed by our team before it goes live** -\nthis usually takes **1–2 business days**. We'll email you as soon as you're\napproved.\n\n> ⚠️ **Heads-up:** You can't open your dashboard until you're approved. That's\n> normal - it keeps the marketplace trustworthy for customers.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Log in\n\nOnce you're approved, go to the login page, enter your **email** and\n**password**, and tap **\"Sign In.\"**\n\n> 💡 Forgot your password? Tap **\"Forgot your password?\"** and we'll email you a\n> reset link.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Pin your shop on the map\n\nThe first time you log in, a **\"Set up your business\"** wizard opens\nautomatically. The most important step is your location: **drag the pin to\nexactly where your shop is.**\n\n![Drag the pin to your exact shop location](/help/screenshots/merchant/03-wizard-location.png)\n\nThis is how customers find you and how we work out delivery fees, so take a\nmoment to get it right. When you see **\"Location saved,\"** tap **\"Next.\"**\n\n> ⚠️ **This step is required.** Your shop won't be visible to customers until\n> your location is pinned.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Add your first product\n\nTap **\"Add your first product\"** to open the product form, then:\n\n![Add your first product - name, photo, and price](/help/screenshots/merchant/05-wizard-product.png)\n\n- **Details:** add a clear **photo**, a **name** (e.g. *Jollof Rice*), and a\n  short **description**.\n- **Pricing:** set the **price** and how much you have in **stock**. (If your\n  item comes in sizes or options, you can add those too.)\n- For food shops, you can add **choices** like protein or sides.\n\nTap **\"Create product.\"** Back in the wizard you'll see **\"First product\nadded!\"** - then tap **\"Complete Setup.\"**\n\n---\n\n## 🎉 You're live!\n\nThat's it - your shop is set up and ready to sell. From your dashboard you can:\n\n- Watch orders arrive in real time under **Orders**\n- Add more items under **Products**\n- Track your money and cash out under **Earnings**\n- Update your hours, location, and password under **Settings**\n\n**Next:** [Receiving & fulfilling orders](/help/merchant/receiving-orders) ·\n[Getting paid](/help/merchant/getting-paid)\n\n> Need a hand? Tap the **\"?\"** help button in your dashboard anytime, or reach\n> support from **Support** in the sidebar.\n"},{"slug":"receiving-orders","title":"Receiving and fulfilling orders","summary":"Accept, prepare, and hand off orders - from new order to rider pickup.","category":"everyday","order":1,"keywords":["orders","incoming orders","new order","accept","reject","process","prepare","ready","ready for pickup","pickup","give to rider","fulfil","fulfill","confirm order","requested","delivered","cancel","modify","receipt","export","status","not getting orders"],"body":"# Receiving and fulfilling orders\n\nEverything that happens after a customer hits \"order\" lives on the **Orders**\npage. This guide walks you through the full journey - from a new order arriving\nto a rider picking it up.\n\n![Your Orders page](/help/screenshots/merchant/orders.png)\n\n---\n\n## How an order moves\n\nEvery order moves through a few clear stages. You handle the first three; Logistics Platform\nhandles the rest.\n\n1. **Requested** - a new order just came in. *(You: accept or reject it.)*\n2. **Accepted** - you've taken the order. *(You: start preparing.)*\n3. **Processing** - you're making it. *(You: mark it ready when packed.)*\n4. **Ready for Pickup** - a rider is called to collect it.\n5. **Rider Assigned → Delivered** - Logistics Platform's rider takes it from here.\n\nNew orders appear **instantly** - watch the little connection indicator at the\ntop-right; when it's green, you're live and receiving in real time.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Accept a new order\n\nWhen an order shows **\"Requested\"** (yellow badge), open it and choose:\n\n- Tap the green **check** to **Accept** it, or\n- Tap the **✕** to **Reject** it (you'll be asked for a reason).\n\n> 💡 Accept quickly - customers see how fast you respond, and a speedy kitchen\n> gets more orders.\n\n## 2. Start preparing\n\nOnce accepted, tap **\"Process\"**. The order moves to **Processing** - this tells\nthe customer you're making their order right now.\n\n## 3. Mark it ready\n\nWhen the order is packed and ready, tap **\"Ready\"**. It becomes **\"Ready for\nPickup\"** and a rider is automatically dispatched to collect it.\n\n> ⚠️ Only mark an order **Ready** when it's genuinely packed - a rider is sent the\n> moment you do.\n\nThat's your part done. You'll see the order update to **Rider Assigned** and\nthen **Delivered** on its own.\n\n---\n\n## Other things you can do with an order\n\n| Button | What it does |\n|---|---|\n| 👁 **View Details** | See the full order - items, customer, delivery address |\n| 🖨 **Print Receipt** | Print a paper receipt for the order |\n| ✏️ **Modify** | Adjust items or add a note (before pickup) |\n| **Cancel** | Cancel an accepted order if you truly can't fulfil it |\n\n## Finding orders\n\n- **Search** by order ID or customer name.\n- Use the **status filter** to show only, say, *Requested* or *Delivered*.\n- **Advanced Filters** let you narrow by date range or order value.\n- **Export** downloads your orders as a CSV or PDF for your records.\n\n> 💡 Got lots of orders at once? Tick several with the checkboxes and use **Accept\n> All** to take them in one go.\n\n---\n\n**Next:** [Getting paid](/help/merchant/getting-paid) ·\n[Adding & managing products](/help/merchant/managing-products)\n"},{"slug":"managing-products","title":"Adding and managing products","summary":"Add items, set prices and variants, hide what's sold out, and edit your catalogue.","category":"everyday","order":2,"keywords":["products","menu","item","menu item","new product","add product","add item","price","change price","stock","variants","sizes","small medium large","options","add-ons","photo","edit","delete","remove","hide","available","sold out","out of stock","catalogue","catalog"],"body":"# Adding and managing products\n\nYour **Products** page is your catalogue - everything customers can order from\nyou. Here's how to add new items, keep them up to date, and hide things when\nyou run out.\n\n![Your Products page](/help/screenshots/merchant/products.png)\n\n---\n\n## Add a new product\n\n1. On the **Products** page, tap **\"New Product\"** (top-right).\n2. The form opens in three quick steps:\n\n![Adding a new product](/help/screenshots/merchant/products-new.png)\n\n   - **Details** - add a **photo**, a **name** (e.g. *Jollof Rice*), and a short\n     **description**. A clear photo helps an item sell.\n   - **Pricing** - set the **price (₦)** and how many you have in **stock**.\n   - **Add-ons** *(food shops only)* - optional choices like protein, sides, or\n     spice level.\n3. Tap **\"Create product.\"**\n\n> 💡 A good photo and a clear name make the biggest difference to sales. Keep\n> descriptions short and appetising.\n\n---\n\n## Products that come in options (sizes, colours, packs)\n\nIf your item comes in **variants** - small/medium/large, different colours, or\npack sizes - turn on **\"Has variants?\"** on the Pricing step. Enter your option\nvalues (e.g. *Small, Medium, Large*), tap **\"Generate combinations,\"** then set a\n**price and stock for each** one.\n\nFor **food add-ons**, create option groups like *\"Pick a protein\"* and add the\nchoices (Chicken, Beef, Fish) with any extra cost. You decide whether a group is\n**required** (customer must pick) or **optional**.\n\n---\n\n## Manage an existing product\n\nEach product shows as a card with three controls:\n\n| Control | What it does |\n|---|---|\n| **Available / Hidden** | Toggle to show or hide the item from customers |\n| **Edit** | Change the name, photo, price, stock, variants, or add-ons |\n| **Delete** | Remove the product permanently |\n\n> 💡 **Sold out for the day?** Don't delete it - just tap **\"Available\"** to flip\n> it to **Hidden**. Flip it back when you restock. Deleting is permanent.\n\nUse the **search box** at the top to find a product quickly when your list grows.\n\n---\n\n**Next:** [Receiving & fulfilling orders](/help/merchant/receiving-orders) ·\n[Getting paid](/help/merchant/getting-paid)\n"},{"slug":"getting-paid","title":"Getting paid: earnings and withdrawals","summary":"Understand your balances and cash out to your bank.","category":"everyday","order":3,"keywords":["earnings","withdraw","withdrawal","cash out","payout","get paid","bank","transfer to bank","available balance","pending","commission","fee","instant","standard","money","wallet","my money","refund"],"body":"# Getting paid: earnings and withdrawals\n\nEvery sale you make lands in your Logistics Platform wallet. The **Earnings** page shows what\nyou've made and lets you cash out to your bank.\n\n![Your Earnings page](/help/screenshots/merchant/earnings.png)\n\n---\n\n## Understanding your balances\n\nAt the top you'll see four cards:\n\n| Card | What it means |\n|---|---|\n| **Available Balance** | Money you can withdraw **right now** |\n| **Pending Balance** | Earnings from orders still being completed (settling soon) |\n| **Total Earnings** | Everything you've earned, all-time |\n| **Total Commission** | The platform fee already deducted from your sales |\n\n> 💡 Money moves from **Pending** to **Available** once an order is delivered and\n> settled. Then it's yours to withdraw.\n\n---\n\n## Withdraw to your bank\n\n1. Tap **\"Request Withdrawal.\"**\n\n![The withdrawal form](/help/screenshots/merchant/earnings-withdraw.png)\n\n2. Enter the **amount**.\n3. Choose how fast you want it:\n   - **Standard** - **free**, arrives within about a day.\n   - **Instant** - arrives in minutes, for a small fee (about 2%).\n4. Enter your **bank**, **account number**, and **account name**.\n5. Confirm.\n\nYou can follow the status anytime under **\"Withdrawal History.\"**\n\n> ⚠️ Withdrawals are a **minimum of ₦1,000** and a **maximum of ₦1,000,000** per\n> request. The **\"Request Withdrawal\"** button is greyed out when your available\n> balance is ₦0.\n\n---\n\n## Refunds and disputes\n\nFrom the Earnings page you can also:\n\n- **Process Refund** - issue a refund to a customer for an order.\n- **Refund History** - see every refund you've made.\n- **Disputes** - review and respond to any payment disputes.\n\nYou can export your transactions to CSV or PDF anytime for your own records using\nthe date-range tools further down the page.\n\n---\n\n**Next:** [Your shop settings](/help/merchant/shop-settings) ·\n[Getting help](/help/merchant/getting-help)\n"},{"slug":"shop-settings","title":"Your shop settings","summary":"Update your profile, hours, open/closed status, notifications, and password.","category":"everyday","order":4,"keywords":["settings","profile","shop name","business info","location","hours","opening times","open","closed","open for orders","go offline","turn off shop","pause shop","notifications","alerts","password","security","login history","category"],"body":"# Your shop settings\n\nThe **Settings** page is where you keep your shop details up to date and manage\nyour account. It's organised into four tabs: **Profile**, **Notifications**,\n**Security**, and **Login History**.\n\n---\n\n## Profile\n\n![Your shop profile settings](/help/screenshots/merchant/settings-profile.png)\n\nThis is your shop's public information. Here you can update:\n\n- **Business name**, **email**, and **phone**\n- **Location** - drag the pin to move where customers find you\n- **Opening** and **Closing** times\n- **Open for orders** - a switch to take your shop online or offline\n- **Description**\n\nTap **\"Save Changes\"** when you're done.\n\n> ⚠️ **\"Open for orders\"** is important: when it's **off**, your shop is hidden\n> from customers and won't receive new orders. Turn it off if you need to close\n> early or take a break, and back on when you're ready again.\n\n> 💡 Your **business category** is shown here but can't be changed yourself -\n> contact support if you need it changed.\n\n---\n\n## Notifications\n\nChoose how you want to be told about activity:\n\n- **Email Notifications** and **Push Notifications** (in your browser)\n- **New Order Alerts** - get pinged the moment an order arrives\n- **Order Status Alerts** - updates as orders progress\n\nKeep **New Order Alerts** on so you never miss an order. Tap **\"Save Changes\"**\nto apply.\n\n---\n\n## Security\n\n![Changing your password](/help/screenshots/merchant/settings-security.png)\n\nChange your password here. Enter your **current password**, then your **new\npassword** twice. A strength meter helps you pick a strong one - use a mix of\nletters, numbers, and symbols.\n\n> 💡 Use a password you don't use anywhere else, and never share it.\n\n---\n\n## Login History\n\nSee recent **logins** (with date, location, and device) and the **devices**\ncurrently signed in to your account. If you spot a login you don't recognise,\nchange your password straight away under **Security**, and contact support.\n\n---\n\n**Next:** [Getting help](/help/merchant/getting-help) ·\n[Troubleshooting & FAQ](/help/merchant/troubleshooting)\n"},{"slug":"getting-help","title":"Getting help: support and disputes","summary":"Raise a support ticket, respond to disputes, and find quick answers.","category":"everyday","order":5,"keywords":["support","help","contact","contact support","customer service","talk to someone","reach us","ticket","raise ticket","complaint","complain","report problem","dispute","customer dispute","refund dispute","faq","knowledge base","issue","problem"],"body":"# Getting help: support and disputes\n\nStuck on something, or a customer has raised an issue? The **Support** page is\nyour direct line to the Logistics Platform team. It has four tabs: **My Tickets**,\n**Disputes**, **FAQ**, and **Knowledge Base**.\n\n![The Support page](/help/screenshots/merchant/support.png)\n\n---\n\n## Raise a support ticket\n\nWhen you need help from the platform team:\n\n1. On the **My Tickets** tab, tap **\"New ticket.\"**\n\n![Creating a support ticket](/help/screenshots/merchant/support-new-ticket.png)\n\n2. Pick a **Category** (Account, Payment, Order, Delivery, Product, Technical, or\n   Other) and a **Priority**.\n3. Add a short **Subject** and **describe the issue** in as much detail as you\n   can.\n4. Optionally **attach a screenshot** - it really speeds things up.\n5. Tap **\"Create ticket.\"**\n\nYour tickets are listed with their status (**Open**, **In Progress**,\n**Resolved**, and so on). Tap any ticket to read replies and continue the\nconversation.\n\n> 💡 The more detail and a screenshot you add up front, the faster we can sort it\n> out.\n\n---\n\n## Disputes\n\nIf a customer disputes one of your orders, it appears under the **Disputes** tab.\nTap a dispute to see the details and **respond with your side** - add any\nevidence you have (photos, notes). The platform team reviews both sides and\ndecides fairly.\n\n> 💡 Respond to disputes promptly and politely with clear evidence - it protects\n> your rating and your earnings.\n\n---\n\n## FAQ and Knowledge Base\n\nBefore raising a ticket, check the **FAQ** and **Knowledge Base** tabs - most\ncommon questions are answered there instantly, no waiting required.\n\n---\n\nYou can also reach us anytime by email at **support@**.\n\n**Next:** [Troubleshooting & FAQ](/help/merchant/troubleshooting)\n"},{"slug":"troubleshooting","title":"Troubleshooting & FAQ","summary":"Quick answers to the most common merchant questions and problems.","category":"troubleshooting","order":1,"keywords":["troubleshooting","faq","problem","not working","cant see my shop","shop not showing","invisible","not found","pending withdrawal","forgot password","otp","verification code","greyed out","disabled","button not working","approval","pending approval","login","help"],"body":"# Troubleshooting & FAQ\n\nQuick answers to the most common questions merchants ask. Can't find yours? Raise\na ticket from **Support**, or email **support@**.\n\n---\n\n## Getting started & access\n\n### Customers can't see my shop\n\nWork through this checklist - it's almost always one of these:\n\n1. **Are you approved?** New accounts are reviewed first (1–2 business days). You\n   can't appear or take orders until you're approved.\n2. **Is your location pinned?** If you skipped pinning your shop on the map,\n   customers can't find you. Set it in **Settings → Profile**.\n3. **Is \"Open for orders\" on?** In **Settings → Profile**, make sure the **Open\n   for orders** switch is on.\n4. **Are you within your opening hours?** Customers can only order between your\n   opening and closing times.\n\n### My account is \"pending approval\" - how long?\n\nUsually **1–2 business days**. We email you the moment you're approved, and then\nyou can log in and finish setting up.\n\n### I can't log in / \"No merchant account is associated with this email\"\n\nThis means the email isn't linked to a merchant account. Double-check you're\nusing the email you **registered as a merchant** with, and that your account has\nbeen **approved**.\n\n### I didn't get my email verification code\n\nCodes arrive within a minute. If not: check your **spam** folder, then tap\n**\"Resend code\"** (you can resend once every 60 seconds). Make sure the email is\nspelled correctly.\n\n### I forgot my password\n\nOn the login screen tap **\"Forgot your password?\"** and we'll email you a reset\nlink. Already logged in? Change it under **Settings → Security**.\n\n---\n\n## Money & withdrawals\n\n### A withdrawal is still pending\n\n**Standard** withdrawals (free) usually arrive within about a day; **instant**\nones (small fee) within minutes. Check **Earnings → Withdrawal History** for the\nstatus. If a standard withdrawal hasn't landed after a couple of business days,\nraise a support ticket.\n\n### The \"Request Withdrawal\" button is greyed out\n\nThat happens when your **Available Balance is ₦0**. Earnings sit in **Pending**\nuntil each order is delivered and settled, then move to **Available** - that's\nwhat you can withdraw.\n\n### What are the withdrawal limits?\n\nMinimum **₦1,000** and maximum **₦1,000,000** per request.\n\n### Why is my balance lower than the order totals?\n\nA small platform **commission** is deducted from each sale - you can see the\ntotal under **Total Commission** on the Earnings page.\n\n---\n\n## Products & orders\n\n### The \"New Product\" button is greyed out\n\nIt's just loading your shop's category - wait a second or two and it'll become\nclickable.\n\n### I've sold out of an item\n\nDon't delete it. On the **Products** page, tap **\"Available\"** on the item to\nflip it to **Hidden**, then flip it back when you restock. Deleting is permanent.\n\n### A new order isn't showing up\n\nCheck the **connection indicator** at the top-right of the **Orders** page - it\nshould be green. Tap the **refresh** button, or reload the page.\n\n### I need to temporarily stop taking orders\n\nTurn off **Open for orders** in **Settings → Profile**. Your shop goes offline\nuntil you turn it back on.\n\n### A customer raised a dispute against my order\n\nOpen it under **Support → Disputes**, and respond with your side and any evidence\n(photos, notes). The team reviews both sides fairly. Respond promptly to protect\nyour rating.\n\n---\n\n## Account\n\n### How do I change my business category?\n\nYou can't change it yourself - contact **support@** and we'll update it\nfor you.\n\n### I saw a login I don't recognise\n\nChange your password immediately under **Settings → Security**, then email\n**support@** so we can help secure your account.\n\n---\n\nStill stuck? Open **Support → New ticket** and include a screenshot - we aim to\nrespond within a few business hours.\n"}]
